Name the specific action and how it landed without blaming their sensitivity, cut every **`but`** that pivots into self-justification, and state what you will do differently going forward.

:::note Office Worked Example (Repair + Dignity Defense)
**Repair:** “In yesterday's review, I jumped in over your analysis and cut off your point. That was wrong—going forward, I'll hold my comments until you finish your walk-through.” · **Dignity Defense:** “When my proposal was dismissed without review, it felt unfair (**Fairness**)—I'd like 10 minutes to walk through the numbers.”
:::

:::note Personal Worked Example (Repairing a Dismissed Boundary)
“When you said you were drained last night, I pushed you to come out instead of respecting your no. I'm sorry—next time you say your battery is low, I'll take it at face value.”
:::

:::note Non-Example (Saving Face / Conditional Apology)
“I'm sorry you felt steamrolled, I was just stressed about the deadline and only meant to help.” *(Centers your stress and puts the feeling on them instead of owning the act.)*
:::

:::note Decision Rule
Put **impact and ownership** ahead of intent; cut any **`but`** that softens your responsibility.
:::

:::dialect Live Dialect Examples
@office_us **Worked Repair (Office US):** Office US: Crisp ownership + period + accountable mechanism + concrete repair.
@personal_us **Worked Repair (Personal US):** Personal US: Warm ownership + affirmation of the bond + zero 'but' or 'sorry you felt'.
@rioplatense **Worked Repair (Rioplatense):** Rioplatense: Warmth and sincerity matter deeply; avoid robotic corporate phrasing with friends.
@espana **Worked Repair (España):** España: Plain, direct ownership without melodrama lands with high credibility.
:::

:::dialect Live Dialect Examples
@office_us **Model Script:** “I steamrolled your point in the budget meeting and cut off your analysis. That was wrong. I got anxious about the clock and jumped in instead of letting you finish. In Thursday's call I'll hand you the floor first—does that work?”
@personal_us **Model Script:** “I went quiet after Thursday instead of telling you I felt stung. That left you guessing, and I'm sorry. I slipped into my old habit of withdrawing when hurt. I value our friendship and want to talk it through—are you up for coffee?”
@rioplatense **Model Script:** “El jueves me cerré y desaparecí en vez de decirte que algo me había dolido. No estuvo bueno dejarte colgado y te pido disculpas. Me importa mucho nuestra amistad—¿charlamos un rato esta semana?”
@espana **Model Script:** “Te interrumpí en la reunión y no te dejé terminar tu planteamiento. Me equivoqué. Me puse nervioso con el tiempo y hablé de más. En la próxima sesión te doy paso primero, ¿te parece bien?”
:::
